# gRPC Development Loop (Agent Rules)

**Canonical doc:** [`docs/guides/grpc-dev-loop.md`](../../docs/guides/grpc-dev-loop.md)

**Do not** read or follow [`docs/plan/Dont-Remove-This-File.txt`](../../docs/plan/Dont-Remove-This-File.txt) — that file is the user's personal scratch notes, not project or agent instructions.

Phase gate scripts chain regressions (`test:grpc:phase11h` → 11G → … → 10I → …). That is correct for **sign-off**, not for every edit.

---

## Three tiers

| Tier | When | Command |
|---|---|---|
| **1 — Edit loop** | After every code change | `npx tsc -b --noEmit` + scoped vitest |
| **2 — Checkpoint** | Before asking user to verify | `npm run test:grpc:fast -- <phase-id>` |
| **3 — Sign-off** | Sub-phase done / merge to `develop` | `npm run test:grpc:phase<phase>` (full chain) |

### Tier 1 commands

```bash
npx tsc -b --noEmit
npx vitest run src/path/to/changed.test.ts
npm run test:grpc:dev              # all gRPC unit tests, no chains
npm run test:grpc:dev:advanced     # Phase 11 scoped
```

### Tier 2 — fast phase gate

```bash
npm run test:grpc:fast -- 11h
# equivalent: GRPC_SKIP_REGRESSION=1 npm run test:grpc:phase11h
```

### Tier 3 — full sign-off only

```bash
npm run test:grpc:phase11h
npm run test:grpc:coverage    # merge gate, if grpc/ touched
npm run test:e2e:grpc         # develop merge gate only
```

---

## Agent mandates

**Do not** during iterative development:

- Run full `test:grpc:phase*` regression chains on every turn
- Audit shipped phases 1–10 unless fixing a reported regression
- Run full E2E or repo-wide 90% coverage sweeps mid-feature
- Repeat monolithic/coverage audit rounds until "no issues" while still implementing

**Do** on every edit batch:

- `npx tsc -b --noEmit`
- Scoped vitest on touched `*.test.ts` files

**Do** before user verify:

- `npm run test:grpc:fast -- <current-phase>`

**Do** at sub-phase sign-off:

- Full `npm run test:grpc:phase<phase>` once

Monolithic (>900 lines) refactors and coverage-gap fixes: scope to files you touch, or run only when the user explicitly requests an audit — not as a gate on every sub-phase commit.

---

## Environment flags

| Variable | Effect |
|---|---|
| `GRPC_SKIP_REGRESSION=1` | Skip chained regressions in phase gate scripts |
| `GRPC_SKIP_TSC=1` | Skip TypeScript (only if you just ran `tsc`) |
| `GRPC_FORCE_TSC=1` | Force TypeScript even if stamp matches HEAD |

Shared helpers live in `scripts/grpc-phase-gate-lib.sh`.
